The containerd journals of a kind node that kind_node_pulls (scripts/e2e/lib/kind-sandbox.sh) reads
in scripts/e2e/lib/kind-sandbox.test.ts, one directory a case, each file named as
kind_sandbox_teardown names a node's journal: containerd-<node>.journal.

The kind job keeps each node's journal of every test as containerd-<node>.journal in its
kind-<leg>-logs artifact, which kind_sandbox_teardown writes with

  docker exec <node> journalctl -u containerd --no-pager -o cat

Three cases are whole journals taken from those artifacts of the kind / rig leg
(TestABurstableGVisorPodOnTheKindRigClonesFromTheFakeGitHub) of workflow_dispatch runs of ci.yaml on
2026-11-24:

- pinned-and-local: run 45300865457 at the branch's head 934b9bc1243c: pulls of
  ghcr.io/cybermonklabs/legion/ci by digest and of the rig's registry; passes.
- refused-pull: run 45304072225, a temporary branch whose rig named docker.io/library/busybox:1.37.0
  for its gVisor check: containerd refused that pull (the node sends every other registry to
  127.0.0.1:1), so it is no pull; passes.
- outside-repository: run 45304089867, a temporary branch whose rig named
  ghcr.io/containerd/busybox:1.36: a pull of ghcr.io in another repository; fails.

Each captured journal has its six lines of containerd's plugin loading taken out whose plugin id
holds the label "internal" between dots, because the repository's private-name rule
(.github/scripts/check-private-names.sh, rule 3) reads such a name as a private host. No line
about a pull was taken out.

One case is written, not captured, because no run leaves a node with no pull:

- no-pull: no PullImage line at all, in the form containerd's CRI plugin logs its start
  (logrus text, the message quoted); fails, as a reader that read nothing.
